From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:56:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] SP: gamepad.cfg follows default.cfg

default.cfg binds keyboard and mouse only. An installation for a gamepad
puts its bindings in a gamepad.cfg (main/ of any search path): it is run
right after default.cfg wherever that is, at the start and when the
controls menu puts everything back to its defaults.
---
 SP/code/qcommon/cmd.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/SP/code/qcommon/cmd.c b/SP/code/qcommon/cmd.c
index 5d06a625..db56aad5 100644
--- a/SP/code/qcommon/cmd.c
+++ b/SP/code/qcommon/cmd.c
@@ -294,6 +294,13 @@ void Cmd_Exec_f( void ) {
 	if (!quiet)
 		Com_Printf ("execing %s\n", filename);
 
+	// the game's default.cfg binds keyboard and mouse only: a gamepad.cfg
+	// next to it (an installation's own, made for its gamepad) follows it
+	// wherever it is run, at the start and when a menu puts the controls
+	// back to their defaults. Cbuf_InsertText puts text first: in reverse.
+	if ( !Q_stricmp( filename, "default.cfg" ) && FS_ReadFile( "gamepad.cfg", NULL ) > 0 )
+		Cbuf_InsertText( "exec gamepad.cfg" );
+
 	Cbuf_InsertText (f.c);
 
 	FS_FreeFile (f.v);
